#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334613 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "466fb505-1ff3-5b27-a5f7-0ea5b31b2927" :knowledge-point/title "Normalizing a Vector in an Inner Product Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3dfca35e-08fe-5bb9-95a9-0f5bac654aa7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(t-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334615} {:answer/id #uuid "c4992185-5ba9-5f5c-a7da-2056e928ccf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}(t-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334616} {:answer/id #uuid "276ad0ba-d974-5558-81bb-fd06f1d2eb03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}(t-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334617} {:answer/id #uuid "ae09c23e-4833-5bda-9f77-cac16120ff3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}(t-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334618} {:answer/id #uuid "8738e785-c246-5d60-8da4-b5069be4fdea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334619}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "276ad0ba-d974-5558-81bb-fd06f1d2eb03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}(t-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334617} :answer-field/id #uuid "748265bd-ac3c-5cab-8148-81ff2d57a7ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334614}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2a226526-c78d-5b45-912b-bc1bae613541" :question/math-academy-id "q-42739" :question/problem "Let $V=C[0,1]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,1],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nNormalize the vector $f(t)=t-1.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨f(t),f(t)⟩}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{(t-1)}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,({t}^{2}-2t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}-{t}^{2}+t)|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-1+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$\n\nTo normalize the vector $f(t),$ we divide $f(t)$ by its norm $‖f(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\frac{f(t)}{‖f(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{t-1}{(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}(t-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186355732 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "090d6747-55e2-548b-84f2-88f6c732518f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector in an Inner Product Space of Continuous Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a237daec-9f6a-57ee-97e5-4630330b3586" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{256}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355734} {:answer/id #uuid "e07da5c9-9c7a-554b-9e60-61edd6f05ef3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355735} {:answer/id #uuid "e1e83e49-c9fc-54bd-8627-2f3e52431ff9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{\\sqrt{15}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355736} {:answer/id #uuid "0a65c723-ecfd-520f-b5bc-2f34d7789242" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355737} {:answer/id #uuid "bf8969fe-d3de-5fe3-9748-568fa6bfc825" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355738}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1e83e49-c9fc-54bd-8627-2f3e52431ff9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{\\sqrt{15}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355736} :answer-field/id #uuid "26a7015b-e5e6-5110-8f91-c272288cf3f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355733}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "30169d9f-5a4b-5d98-acdf-194d4d7ec50a" :question/math-academy-id "q-42763" :question/problem "Let $V=C[0,2]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,2],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $f(t)=t+{t}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨f(t),f(t)⟩}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(f(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(t+{t}^{2})^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({t}^{2}+2{t}^{3}+{t}^{4})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{{t}^{4}}{2}+\\frac{{t}^{5}}{5})|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}+8+\\frac{32}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{256}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{\\frac{256}{15}}=\\frac{16}{\\sqrt{15}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334641 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e023193-7494-5e3a-bd6e-e15ae0e9a1bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector in an Inner Product Space of Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "750755aa-f8a3-5df4-a17e-a8d5870332ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334643} {:answer/id #uuid "6ca2c068-09ad-5d1e-839d-9360e6a66e45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334644} {:answer/id #uuid "09883923-2498-5111-860f-c25f2316de28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334645} {:answer/id #uuid "0daa0b98-90e6-5a8f-9b1c-06d96399bc43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334646} {:answer/id #uuid "b96e8328-ba05-5880-9ee9-67946f7f46a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ca2c068-09ad-5d1e-839d-9360e6a66e45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334644} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1102dc6-9fea-5714-9894-b2c091908038" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334642}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "65d60515-7767-5b6f-afb5-20fa2b5f3e11" :question/math-academy-id "q-97417" :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(1)y(1)+x(0)y(0)+x(-1)y(-1).\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $p(t)=2t-{t}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $p(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $p(t)=2t-{t}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(1)=1,\\,p(0)=0,\\,p(-1)=-3.\n$$\n\nComputing $‖p(t)‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{p(1)p(1)+p(0)p(0)+p(-1)p(-1)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{[p(1)]^{2}+[p(0)]^{2}+[p(-1)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+(0)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+0+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186355739 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e023193-7494-5e3a-bd6e-e15ae0e9a1bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector in an Inner Product Space of Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d32bb559-2b81-5393-860a-1283266fe2b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{105}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355741} {:answer/id #uuid "f4183ccc-bcb7-58f6-9c3a-5ac61900f2b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{115}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355742} {:answer/id #uuid "6c5123ec-b63c-59a4-87a5-37d261efb433" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355743} {:answer/id #uuid "88f7ec97-011d-5439-9aa6-348d1703d4dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355744} {:answer/id #uuid "a6bf2e42-d063-5c65-9c6c-7e8e09a41ede" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355745}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4183ccc-bcb7-58f6-9c3a-5ac61900f2b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{115}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355742} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf5e903a-5ce8-5190-a15e-7b3cce6b0034" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355740}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b37d5348-c5f2-5d7d-bfb2-33bef9089323" :question/math-academy-id "q-97426" :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(-2)y(-2)+x(0)y(0)+x(2)y(2).\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $p(t)=3-t+{t}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $p(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $p(t)=3-t+{t}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(-2)=9,\\,p(0)=3,\\,p(2)=5.\n$$\n\nComputing $‖p(t)‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{p(-2)p(-2)+p(0)p(0)+p(2)p(2)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{[p(-2)]^{2}+[p(0)]^{2}+[p(2)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(9)^{2}+(3)^{2}+(5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{81+9+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{115}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186355746 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "466fb505-1ff3-5b27-a5f7-0ea5b31b2927" :knowledge-point/title "Normalizing a Vector in an Inner Product Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa3833c7-7c3f-5b3c-9000-c0156dfd78f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{31}}{31}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355748} {:answer/id #uuid "70db83a4-bda6-5ff6-9d51-054750eb4c2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{14}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355749} {:answer/id #uuid "8e6314bc-4937-5ddc-89b1-27e04e346d45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{13}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355750} {:answer/id #uuid "c7d81493-e5b0-57c0-8153-c142c975537e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355751} {:answer/id #uuid "9de771eb-62e3-5330-8685-6539c304fc37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355752}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa3833c7-7c3f-5b3c-9000-c0156dfd78f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{31}}{31}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355748} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ed3ffe0-7be0-59e9-907f-a2033c2cdad5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355747}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "89dfaeb6-595c-5446-b274-cea99af3ddca" :question/math-academy-id "q-97724" :question/problem "An inner product on $V={R}^{3}$ is defined as $⟨x,y⟩={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.$ \n\nNormalize the  vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ under this inner product." :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $v$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖=\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨v,v⟩ & =1\\cdot 1+3\\cdot (2\\cdot 2)+2\\cdot (3\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =1+12+18 \\\\  & =31.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{31}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo normalize the vector $v$, we divide $v$ by its norm $‖v‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{v}{‖v‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{31}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{31}}{31}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
